Description: Nonparametric estimation and inference for second-order Markov
    multistate models in discrete time. Provides the relative probability
    estimator (RPE) of the 1-step second-order homogeneous transition
    probabilities, together with consistent variance estimators, confidence
    intervals, an extension of the Chapman-Kolmogorov relation for n-step
    prediction, and evolution intervals.
    Also provides a discrete-time complementary log-log cause-specific hazard
    regression for the covariate-adjusted transition probabilities (with
    time-varying and duration-dependent baselines and covariate-adjusted
    multi-step prediction), Wald and likelihood-ratio tests of the first-order
    Markov assumption, subject-level bootstrap intervals for multi-step
    predictions, a first-order discrete baseline and tools to compare first-
    and second-order predictions across all transitions, data preparation
    from 'mstate'-style wide data, and 'probtrans'-compatible output.
    The package complements 'mstate' by adding a second-order (short-memory)
    layer to the classical first-order multistate framework. Methods are
    described in Najera-Zuloaga, Besalu and Gomez Melis (2025, in review) and
    build on Besalu and Gomez Melis (2024) "Second order Markov multistate
    models", SORT, 48(2), 209-234.
